<task id="074" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Outlook add-in save pane consumes Association Engine suggestions (show + accept/override)</title>
    <phase>Wave 7 — Microsoft hardening + auth + index</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>072, 012</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>office-addins</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Makes the add-in save pane a consumer of the server Association Engine — new client feature calling a BFF suggestion surface, rendering confidence + provenance, and applying an accepted/overridden association. `office-addins` tag + auth-gated BFF call trigger FULL rigor; must respect ADR-028 (NAA auth via task 072) and the review-surface auth-scoping (NFR-07).</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W7</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Depends on 072 (add-in NAA foundation) and 012 (deterministic rungs producing suggestions). Touches the add-in save pane only; runs after both land. Client feature over an existing BFF suggestion path.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-25</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Make the Outlook add-in save task pane a consumer of the Association Engine (W1). When the user saves an email via the add-in, call the BFF (under NAA auth from task 072) to obtain the engine's association suggestions for that communication and render them in the save pane: suggested target record(s), confidence, and provenance rationale. The user can accept the top suggestion in one click or override by picking another target. The accepted/overridden association is applied to the resulting `sprk_communication` (via the same regarding machinery the Code Page review path uses — no new regarding mechanism).

    This mirrors the W4 Code Page review surface (task 042) but inside Outlook. Reuse the engine's suggestion contract; do NOT re-implement association logic client-side. Respect matter-level auth scoping (NFR-07) — the pane only shows suggestions the caller is authorized to see; AI-flagged privilege is surfaced, never decided.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Office Add-ins engineer authoritative on the Outlook save task pane, the `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy` auth path (task 072), and the Association Engine suggestion contract (W1 tasks 011–012). Familiar with the regarding machinery (`RegardingResolver`/`PolymorphicResolverService`) reused on accept.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The add-in save pane fetches and displays engine suggestions (target + confidence + provenance) for the saved email; the user accepts in one click or overrides by selecting another target; the chosen association is applied to the `sprk_communication`. Auth-scoped per NFR-07; privilege flagged not decided. Add-in builds + deploys via `office-addins-deploy`; the flow is smoke-tested in dev.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Completes the FR-25 add-in track: task 072 wired NAA + manifest, task 073 protected the BFF Office endpoints, and this task turns the save pane into a review surface over the Association Engine so users can confirm/override associations without leaving Outlook. It parallels the Code Page review path (task 042) — same engine, same regarding machinery, different host.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/office-addins/ (Outlook save task pane)</file>
